#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-failures — the box's failure ledger, apart from the board: one JSON line per failure, counted on read.
Design: docs/design-failure-noticing-2026-09-11.md (The failures board, The rule). Nothing here launches, queues,
proposes or posts: the ledger is written, counted and rendered, no more.

usage: cc-failures record --scope S --kind CONTRACT/SYMPTOM --observed TEXT [--expected TEXT] [--evidence TEXT]...
                          [--detector box|person|unknown] [--detector-evidence TEXT] [--writer W] [--cost k=v]...
                          [--link k=v]... [--critical REASON] [--status confirmed|asserted|refuted] [--ts UTC]
                          [--corrects ID] [--once]
       cc-failures show [--scope S] [--as-of UTC] [--all] [ID]   (--json: the records, corrections folded in)
       cc-failures eligible [--scope S] [--as-of UTC]
       cc-failures claim [--scope S] [--as-of UTC] [--dry]      (one eligible cluster, claimed once; the launch's call)
       cc-failures recurring [claim [--dry] | held --scope S --text TEXT] [--scope S] [--as-of UTC]
                                                        (gate cases red on landing after landing: RECURRING)
       cc-failures packet ID                                   (the investigation's packet, markdown; ID a claim or a cluster)
       cc-failures metrics [FIXTURE] [--scope S]        (the shipped one: tests/failures-fixture.jsonl)
       cc-failures replay [EVENTS] [--catalogue JSON] [--candidate EXE] [--candidate-catalogue JSON] [--json]
                                                        (the shipped one: tests/failures-replay.jsonl)
       cc-failures import REPO [--dry]
       cc-failures kinds
       cc-failures board REPO [--as-of UTC]                 (what `cc board failures REPO` runs)
       cc-failures selfcheck

THE LEDGER is ~/.cc/failures/<scope>.jsonl (CC_FAILURES points it elsewhere; a test run keeps out of the box's own),
append-only, one line per record, written under a lock. Records are immutable; a correction is a record of its
own (`record --corrects ID --status refuted|confirmed`) and every read folds the latest one in. Clusters and counts
are computed on read, never stored. `record --once` is for a writer that sees the same failure every tick: it needs
`--link source=KEY`, and when the scope already holds a record with that source it writes nothing and prints
`already <id>`. The read and the append are not one lock, so a writer that can race itself holds its own.

THE RECORD: ts (when it happened, UTC), filed (when it was written), scope, kind, fingerprint (`v1|<scope>|<kind>`)
and its id `c-<hash>`, expected, observed, evidence (paths, refs, excerpts), detector ({who: box|person|unknown,
evidence}), writer, cost (a list; unknown stays unknown, never summed), links (row, pr, thread, journal, source,
episode), status (confirmed|asserted|refuted), critical (a reason from the catalogue, or empty).

THE KIND is `<contract>/<symptom>`: the broken contract and what was seen, never the guessed cause. The catalogue
is config/failure-kinds.json beside this bin (`kinds` prints it; CC_FAILURES_CATALOGUE names another — a test's, or
the one `replay` scores); a kind not in it is accepted and said, so the
catalogue grows by use — but a typo splits a cluster, so read `kinds` first.

THE RULE (arithmetic, evaluated on read, `--as-of` replays it at another time):
    eligible = a critical record in the last 14 days
            OR distinct confirmed episodes of the fingerprint in the last 14 days >= 3
An episode is a run of records of one fingerprint closer than 30 minutes to each other: the same failure written
twice in a minute is one episode. A refuted record counts nowhere; an asserted one (a candidate) counts nowhere
until confirmed. After fourteen quiet days a cluster leaves the active view (`--all` shows it); its records stay.

THE CLAIM (docs: The investigation). `claim` hands back a claim whose investigation did not happen and is due again
(below, writing nothing); failing that it takes the first eligible cluster nobody holds and writes one line to
~/.cc/failures/claims.jsonl (`i-<hash>`, the finding id). Either way it prints `<claim>\t<cluster>\t<scope>\t<kind>\t<why>\t<slot>`
and exits 1 with a reason on stderr when there is nothing to claim. One claim per cluster per 14 days — later
instances attach; a cluster still eligible 14 days on is a repeat and may be claimed again. Two a rolling day, by
slot: one `routine` (any cluster) and one `critical` (a cluster with a critical record; it may take the routine slot
too). The claim is the ledger's whole part in an investigation: the tier check, the launch and the report belong to
whoever runs `cc-audit failure <claim>` (cc-reconcile's tick, one at a time), and the report lands at
~/.cc/failures/reports/<claim>.md.
A REPORT IS NOT ALWAYS A RESULT. cc-audit writes one whether or not the investigation happened, so that a cluster
nobody could investigate stays visible; when it did not happen the report opens with
`**Not investigated (deferred|failed):** <why> · again after <stamp>` and this file reads that line. Deferred = a pass
refused or postponed by a limit: nothing ran and nothing was spent. Failed = a pass that ran and failed: a result, and
it cost money. Either way the SAME claim is offered again once its stamp has passed — no new claims line, no slot
spent, the way cc-land defers a usage-limited review (`attempts - 1`, stage deferred) — because a claim reading
`reported` for work that never happened is a gravestone the cluster never comes back from. A handback yields
rather than starve work nobody has looked at: `deferred` to a free critical cluster (claimed the day it
crosses), `failed` to any free cluster, since that one ran and cost money. `show`,
`eligible` and `board` say `claimed <when> <claim>` (then `reported`, or `deferred`/`failed` with the stamp it comes
back at) or `unclaimed <age>`, the age
counted from the moment the rule fired, so a cluster nobody may investigate stays visible with its age. `packet`
prints what the investigation reads: the count, span, writers, detectors and costs, the first, the crossing and the
newest record, at most six excerpts of distinct evidence, and the scope's other clusters.

RECURRING (cc-reconcile's THE DEEP FIX). A `gate-verdict/red` record is one fingerprint for every gate, so the CASE
is read out of it: each ✗/✘/FAIL/not ok line of its excerpt's red section (both writers keep one; the observed text
when there is none), with paths, shas and numbers taken out, keyed by scope and gate. A LANDING is the record's PR,
else its tree, so one PR re-run counts once. `recurring` lists the cases in the last CC_RECURRING_RED_WINDOW_H hours
(72) with their landings; `recurring claim` takes the first case red on CC_RECURRING_RED_MIN landings (3) that no
claim holds, writes one line to ~/.cc/failures/recurring/claims.jsonl and prints it as JSON (exit 1 and why on stderr
when there is none). A claim holds its case for CC_RECURRING_RED_COOL_H hours (24), and past that while its worker's
journal (<CC_STATE>/<scope>/<track>/progress.md) has no STATUS line and moved inside two cool-downs; a held-then-freed
case is claimed again only when it has gone red on the threshold again since its claim. Two claims a rolling day,
whatever the cases. `recurring held` exits 0 and names the claim when every case a landing's red text names is held.
The three thresholds are cc-config keys (the environment wins). Nothing here launches: cc-reconcile does.

PERSON-FIRST: `--detector person` writes the record AND a `failure-detection/person-first` record beside it,
critical, linked by `links.episode` — a person catching a failure the box did not record is critical every time,
and the gap is a failure of its own that stays out of the failure count.

IMPORT reads a board (through cc-board, never the file) and the briefs under CC_STATE: every `raised-` row is a
record at its filing time; every note or brief line marked INSTANCE (the word, singular) is a record at the time it states (
`2026-09-07 19:0xZ`, `17:2xZ`, `17:12 PDT`; none stated: the note's time), filed at the note's time; "again" in a
note is a lead, not a count. A row files under the first catalogue kind whose `match` regex hits its name, else
under its own family `board-row/<row>`. Idempotent on links.source. The rows stay the work they are.

METRICS with no argument reads the ledger: records, clusters, eligible, recording delay (filed − ts, minutes),
the unknown-detector and person-first shares. With a labelled fixture (JSONL: label, row, text, filed, ts) it runs
the import's own classifier and time parser over each line and prints the false-match rate (pairs grouped
together whose labels differ), the false-split rate (pairs of one label grouped apart), the share of stated times
recovered, and the recording delay.

REPLAY scores a detector change on pinned raw events before it touches the live ledger (docs: Phased plan, phase 3).
EVENTS is a frozen JSONL of events as their writers would have written them — `ts`, `filed`, `scope`, `text`, and
either `kind` (a session's line) or `row` (a board's, classified by the catalogue under test), plus `detector`,
`critical`, `status`, `label` and `control` as needed; the shipped one is September's, from the design's evidence, under the neutral scope `box` with names scrubbed.
Each run plays the events in order into a temporary ledger of its own — the live one is never read or written —
and asks the rule after every event, so a cluster's `fired` is the first moment the rule would have said so. The
BASELINE is this executable with its catalogue (`--catalogue` swaps it); the CANDIDATE is `--candidate EXE`
(another cc-failures, run as `EXE replay EVENTS --json`), `--candidate-catalogue JSON` (this one with that
catalogue), or both. It prints what each would have fired and when, what stayed quiet, and the difference: fired
by one and not the other, and a crossing that moved. NEGATIVE CONTROLS are events whose `control` names why their
cluster must stay quiet (one episode written three times, two episodes, three across fifteen days, candidates
never confirmed, a refuted critical); a control cluster holds control events only, and a run in which one fires
— or a control that shares a cluster with a real event — exits 1, so a candidate that fires on a control is not
scored green. No model call, no board, no claim: `replay` writes nothing outside its temporary directory."""
import sys, os, re, json, fcntl, hashlib, datetime, subprocess, statistics, tempfile, shutil, collections, time

B = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
DIR = os.environ.get("CC_FAILURES") or os.path.expanduser("~/.cc/failures")
STATE = os.environ.get("CC_STATE") or os.path.expanduser("~/.cc/state")
CATALOGUE = os.environ.get("CC_FAILURES_CATALOGUE") or os.path.join(B, "..", "config", "failure-kinds.json")   # replay swaps it per run
FIXTURE = os.path.join(B, "..", "tests", "failures-fixture.jsonl")   # the labelled fixture `metrics` is measured on
EVENTS = os.path.join(B, "..", "tests", "failures-replay.jsonl")     # the pinned raw events `replay` scores a detector on
WINDOW_DAYS = 14          # "in the last 14 days"
EPISODES_NEEDED = 3       # "three distinct episodes"
EPISODE_GAP_MIN = 30      # records of one fingerprint closer than this are one episode
STATUSES = ("confirmed", "asserted", "refuted")
DETECTORS = ("box", "person", "unknown")
GAP_KIND = "failure-detection/person-first"
FP_VERSION = "v1"
SLOTS = {"routine": 1, "critical": 1}   # claims per rolling day, by slot: "one routine and one extra critical per rolling day"
DAY = 86400

def die(msg, rc=2):
    print(f"cc-failures: {msg}", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(rc)
def utc(dt): return dt.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
def now_dt(): return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)
def parse_ts(s):
    """`2026-09-11T17:20Z`, `2026-09-11T17:20:00Z`, `2026-09-11 17:20` → aware UTC datetime; None when it is not one."""
    if not s: return None
    s = s.strip().replace(" ", "T")
    for fmt in ("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M"):
        try: return datetime.datetime.strptime(s, fmt).replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
        except ValueError: pass
    return None

def catalogue():
    try:
        with open(CATALOGUE) as f: return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e: die(f"catalogue {CATALOGUE}: {e}")

def fingerprint(scope, kind): return f"{FP_VERSION}|{scope}|{kind}"
def fpid(fp): return "c-" + hashlib.sha1(fp.encode()).hexdigest()[:8]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ledger: append under a lock, read and fold
SCOPE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$")   # a board's name; never a path
def _path(scope):
    if not SCOPE.match(scope) or scope == "claims": die(f"scope is a workspace or project name, got '{scope}'")   # claims.jsonl is the claim ledger, never a scope
    return os.path.join(DIR, f"{scope}.jsonl")
def append(scope, rec):
    os.makedirs(DIR, exist_ok=True)
    line = json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n"
    with open(_path(scope), "a") as f:
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        f.write(line); f.flush(); os.fsync(f.fileno())
def scopes():
    if not os.path.isdir(DIR): return []
    return sorted(fn[:-6] for fn in os.listdir(DIR) if fn.endswith(".jsonl") and fn != "claims.jsonl")
def load(scope=None):
    """Every record, corrections folded in: a record with `corrects` sets the status of the record it names (the
    latest correction wins) and is not itself a record. Unreadable lines are said on stderr and skipped."""
    recs, corr = [], []
    for s in ([scope] if scope else scopes()):
        p = _path(s)
        if not os.path.isfile(p): continue
        with open(p) as f:
            for n, line in enumerate(f, 1):
                line = line.strip()
                if not line: continue
                try: r = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError: print(f"cc-failures: {p}:{n}: not JSON, skipped", file=sys.stderr); continue
                (corr if r.get("corrects") else recs).append(r)
    by = {r["id"]: r for r in recs}
    for c in sorted(corr, key=lambda c: c.get("ts", "")):
        if c["corrects"] in by:
            by[c["corrects"]]["status"] = c["status"]; by[c["corrects"]].setdefault("corrections", []).append(c["id"])
    return recs

def claims_path(): return os.path.join(DIR, "claims.jsonl")
def report_path(claim_id): return os.path.join(DIR, "reports", f"{claim_id}.md")
# The line cc-audit opens a report with when the investigation did not happen (A REPORT IS NOT ALWAYS A RESULT, above).
# Anchored at the start of the file, so a report that merely QUOTES the wording lower down is still a report.
# The why is left where the reader is: in the report itself. This reads the two facts it acts on — which state, and when.
NOT_INVESTIGATED = re.compile(r"\A\*\*Not investigated \((deferred|failed)\):\*\* .+? · again after (\S+)\s*$", re.M)
def report_state(claim_id):
    """('investigated'|'deferred'|'failed', again-datetime-or-None) for a claim's report, or None when there is no file."""
    p = report_path(claim_id)
    if not os.path.isfile(p): return None
    try:
        with open(p, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f: head = f.read(600)
    except OSError: return None
    m = NOT_INVESTIGATED.search(head)
    return (m.group(1), parse_ts(m.group(2))) if m else ("investigated", None)
def claims():
    p = claims_path()
    if not os.path.isfile(p): return []
    out = []
    with open(p) as f:
        for n, line in enumerate(f, 1):
            if not line.strip(): continue
            try: out.append(json.loads(line))
            except ValueError: print(f"cc-failures: {p}:{n}: not JSON, skipped", file=sys.stderr)
    return out
def append_claim(rec):
    os.makedirs(DIR, exist_ok=True)
    with open(claims_path(), "a") as f:
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        f.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n"); f.flush(); os.fsync(f.fileno())
def held(cid, ks, as_of):
    """The claim holding cluster `cid` as of `as_of`: the newest one younger than the window, else None."""
    mine = [k for k in ks if k.get("cluster") == cid and parse_ts(k.get("ts")) and
            0 <= (as_of - parse_ts(k["ts"])).total_seconds() < WINDOW_DAYS * DAY]
    return max(mine, key=lambda k: k["ts"]) if mine else None
def age(a, b):
    m = int((a - b).total_seconds() // 60)
    return f"{m // 1440}d {m % 1440 // 60}h" if m >= 1440 else (f"{m // 60}h {m % 60}m" if m >= 60 else f"{m}m")

def new_id(seed=None):
    seed = seed or os.urandom(8).hex()
    return "f-" + hashlib.sha1(seed.encode()).hexdigest()[:10]

def add_record(scope, kind, observed, expected="", evidence=(), detector="unknown", detector_evidence="",
               writer="session", cost=(), links=None, critical="", status="confirmed", ts=None, filed=None,
               source=None, dry=False, corrects=None):
    """One record, and — for a person-first one — its gap record beside it. Returns the ids written.
    `corrects`: this line is a correction of that record (its new status is `status`), not a record of its own."""
    cat = catalogue()
    if "/" not in kind or kind.startswith("/") or kind.endswith("/"): die(f"kind is <contract>/<symptom>, got '{kind}'")
    if detector not in DETECTORS: die(f"detector is one of {'|'.join(DETECTORS)}, got '{detector}'")
    if status not in STATUSES: die(f"status is one of {'|'.join(STATUSES)}, got '{status}'")
    if critical and critical not in cat["critical"]: die(f"critical is one of {'|'.join(cat['critical'])}, got '{critical}'")
    if not observed.strip(): die("observed is empty: say what was seen")
    if kind not in cat["kinds"] and not kind.startswith("board-row/"):
        print(f"cc-failures: '{kind}' is not in the catalogue ({os.path.normpath(CATALOGUE)}); recorded as a kind of its own", file=sys.stderr)
    ts = ts or now_dt(); filed = filed if filed is not None else now_dt()
    fp = fingerprint(scope, kind)
    rec = {"id": new_id(source), "ts": utc(ts), "filed": utc(filed) if filed else "", "scope": scope, "kind": kind,
           "fingerprint": fp, "cluster": fpid(fp), "expected": expected, "observed": observed, "evidence": list(evidence),
           "detector": {"who": detector, "evidence": detector_evidence}, "writer": writer, "cost": list(cost),
           "links": dict(links or {}), "status": status, "critical": critical}
    if source: rec["links"]["source"] = source
    if corrects: rec["corrects"] = corrects
    ids = [rec["id"]]
    if not dry: append(scope, rec)
    # "Every person-first episode is a record of its own, failure-detection/person-first, critical, and points at the
    # original episode": written here, once, beside the episode — never for the gap record itself.
    if detector == "person" and kind != GAP_KIND and not corrects:
        gk = cat["kinds"].get(GAP_KIND, {})
        gap = dict(rec); gap["id"] = new_id((source or rec["id"]) + "#gap"); gap["kind"] = GAP_KIND
        gap["fingerprint"] = fingerprint(scope, GAP_KIND); gap["cluster"] = fpid(gap["fingerprint"])
        gap["expected"] = gk.get("contract", ""); gap["observed"] = f"a person found, not the box: {observed}"
        gap["critical"] = "person-first"; gap["links"] = dict(rec["links"], episode=rec["id"])
        if source: gap["links"]["source"] = source + "#gap"
        ids.append(gap["id"])
        if not dry: append(scope, gap)
    return ids

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the count: episodes, clusters, the rule
def episodes(recs):
    """Records of ONE fingerprint → episodes: a new one starts when the gap from the previous record is over
    EPISODE_GAP_MIN, compared at the minute the stamps are written to."""
    out = []
    for r in sorted(recs, key=lambda r: r["ts"]):
        t = parse_ts(r["ts"]).replace(second=0)
        if out and (t - out[-1][-1]).total_seconds() < EPISODE_GAP_MIN * 60: out[-1].append(t)   # closer than: 30 apart is a new one
        else: out.append([t])
    return out

def clusters(recs, as_of=None, ks=None):
    """Group by fingerprint and apply the rule as of `as_of` (default now). Records after as_of are not seen.
    `ks`: the claims (read once by the caller), so each eligible cluster knows who holds it."""
    as_of = as_of or now_dt(); ks = claims() if ks is None else ks
    since = as_of - datetime.timedelta(days=WINDOW_DAYS)
    by = {}
    for r in recs:
        if parse_ts(r["ts"]) is None or parse_ts(r["ts"]) > as_of: continue
        by.setdefault(r["fingerprint"], []).append(r)
    out = []
    for fp, rs in by.items():
        live = [r for r in rs if r.get("status") == "confirmed"]
        recent = [r for r in live if parse_ts(r["ts"]) >= since]
        crit = [r for r in recent if r.get("critical")]
        eps = episodes(live); eps14 = [e for e in eps if e[-1] >= since.replace(second=0)]   # any record of it in the window
        # THE RULE, verbatim: "eligible = critical OR distinct confirmed episodes of the fingerprint in the last 14 days >= 3"
        why = f"critical: {crit[0]['critical']}" if crit else (f"{len(eps14)} episodes in {WINDOW_DAYS}d" if len(eps14) >= EPISODES_NEEDED else "")
        # when the rule fired: the critical record's own time, or the first stamp of the third episode in the window
        crossed = min(r["ts"] for r in crit) if crit else (utc(eps14[EPISODES_NEEDED - 1][0]) if why else "")
        stamps = sorted(r["ts"] for r in live) or sorted(r["ts"] for r in rs)
        cid = fpid(fp); k = held(cid, ks, as_of) if why else None
        rep = report_state(k["id"]) if k else None   # the file is not the answer: what it SAYS is (A REPORT IS NOT ALWAYS A RESULT)
        out.append({"id": cid, "fingerprint": fp, "scope": rs[0]["scope"], "kind": rs[0]["kind"],
                    "records": len(rs), "confirmed": len(live), "episodes": len(eps), "episodes_14d": len(eps14),
                    "critical": len(crit), "eligible": why, "crossed": crossed, "active": bool(recent),
                    "first": stamps[0] if stamps else "", "last": stamps[-1] if stamps else "",
                    "person_first": sum(1 for r in live if r["detector"]["who"] == "person"),
                    "claim": k, "report": rep, "reported": bool(rep and rep[0] == "investigated")})
    out.sort(key=lambda c: (not c["eligible"], -c["episodes_14d"], c["kind"]))
    return out

def claim_word(c, as_of=None):
    """What show/eligible/board say beside an eligible cluster: who holds it, or how long nobody has."""
    if not c["eligible"]: return ""
    if c["claim"]:
        word = f"claimed {c['claim']['ts'][:16]} {c['claim']['id']}"
        if c["reported"]: return word + " reported"
        # An investigation that did not happen says so, and when it comes back: the cluster stays visible as
        # un-investigated instead of reading `reported` off a file that stands for nothing.
        if c["report"]: return word + f" {c['report'][0]}, again after {utc(c['report'][1]) if c['report'][1] else 'the next claim'}"
        return word
    return f"unclaimed {age(as_of or now_dt(), parse_ts(c['crossed']))}"

def claim_one(scope=None, as_of=None, dry=False):
    """A claim whose investigation did not happen and is due again (handed back as it stands, nothing written), or
    the first eligible cluster nobody holds within the day's slots → the claim (written unless dry), or None with the
    reason on stderr. Which of the two goes first is the yielding rule below.
    Never touches a scope ledger: recording stays what it was."""
    as_of = as_of or now_dt(); ks = claims()
    cl = [c for c in clusters(load(scope), as_of, ks) if c["eligible"]]
    # a free critical cluster is claimed before any non-critical one — the guard above tests the same order
    # (a free critical cluster) — a stable sort keeps cl's -episodes_14d order within each class.
    free = sorted((c for c in cl if not c["claim"]), key=lambda c: not c["critical"])
    today = [k for k in ks if parse_ts(k.get("ts")) and 0 <= (as_of - parse_ts(k["ts"])).total_seconds() < DAY]
    used = {slot: sum(1 for k in today if k.get("slot") == slot) for slot in SLOTS}
    # a critical cluster takes the critical slot, or the routine one when that is free; a routine cluster only the routine one
    def slot_for(c): return next((sl for sl in (("critical", "routine") if c["critical"] else ("routine",)) if used[sl] < SLOTS[sl]), None)
    # A DEFERRED OR FAILED INVESTIGATION DID NOT USE THE CLAIM UP: the SAME claim is handed back once its `again after`
    # has passed. No new line and no second slot — the way cc-land defers a usage-limited review (attempts - 1, stage
    # deferred). AT the stamp it is offered: the stamp is when the reason to wait ended, not the first second after.
    # A HANDBACK NEVER STARVES A CLUSTER NOBODY HAS LOOKED AT. A broad pass that fails the same way every time — a
    # packet too big for the $0.60 cap — re-stamps itself a day on, so an unbounded handback would hold the slot for
    # the whole 14-day window and a critical cluster crossing tomorrow would wait it out. So it yields:
    #   a `deferred` handback yields to a free CRITICAL cluster that can take a slot — a critical cluster is claimed
    #     the day it crosses — but not to routine work: nothing ran and nothing was spent, and the limit that stopped
    #     it stops a fresh claim too, so spending the slot on new work buys another refusal;
    #   a `failed` handback yields to ANY free cluster that can take a slot: it ran and it cost money, and a cluster
    #     nobody has looked at is the better use of the slot. It stays visible as `failed` meanwhile, never `reported`.
    back = [c for c in cl if c["report"] and c["report"][0] != "investigated"
            and (c["report"][1] is None or c["report"][1] <= as_of)]
    deferred = next((c for c in back if c["report"][0] == "deferred"), None)
    failed = next((c for c in back if c["report"][0] == "failed"), None)
    if deferred and not any(c["critical"] and slot_for(c) for c in free): return deferred["claim"]
    if failed and not any(slot_for(c) for c in free): return failed["claim"]
    for c in free:
        slot = slot_for(c)
        if not slot: continue
        k = {"id": "i-" + hashlib.sha1(f"{c['id']}|{utc(as_of)}".encode()).hexdigest()[:8], "ts": utc(as_of), "cluster": c["id"],
             "scope": c["scope"], "kind": c["kind"], "why": c["eligible"], "slot": slot, "critical": bool(c["critical"])}
        if not dry: append_claim(k)
        return k
    why = (f"{len(cl)} eligible, {len(cl) - len(free)} claimed" + (f", the day's {'/'.join(sl for sl in SLOTS if used[sl] >= SLOTS[sl])} slot(s) used" if free else "")) if cl else "nothing eligible"
    print(f"cc-failures: nothing to claim: {why}", file=sys.stderr)
    return None

def packet(ident, as_of=None):
    """The investigation's packet (docs: The investigation, step 1), for a claim id or a cluster id."""
    ks = claims(); k = next((x for x in ks if x.get("id") == ident), None)
    cid = k["cluster"] if k else ident
    recs = [r for r in load() if r["cluster"] == cid]
    if not recs: die(f"no claim or cluster {ident}")
    scope = recs[0]["scope"]; as_of = as_of or now_dt()
    k = k or held(cid, ks, as_of)   # by cluster id: the claim holding it now, if any
    cl = clusters(load(scope), as_of, ks); c = next((x for x in cl if x["id"] == cid), None)
    if not c: die(f"cluster {cid} has no record as of {utc(as_of)}")
    cat = catalogue().get("kinds", {}).get(c["kind"], {})
    live = sorted((r for r in recs if r["status"] == "confirmed" and parse_ts(r["ts"]) <= as_of), key=lambda r: r["ts"])
    if not live: die(f"cluster {cid} has no confirmed record")
    def rec(r, tag):
        L = [f"### {tag}: {r['id']}  {r['ts']}  writer {r['writer']}  detector {r['detector']['who']}" + (f"  CRITICAL ({r['critical']})" if r["critical"] else ""),
             f"expected: {r['expected'] or '(not stated)'}", f"observed: {r['observed']}"]
        if r["evidence"]: L.append("evidence: " + " · ".join(r["evidence"]))
        if r["links"]: L.append("links: " + " · ".join(f"{a}={b}" for a, b in r["links"].items()))
        if r["cost"]: L.append("cost: " + ", ".join(r["cost"]))
        if r["detector"].get("evidence"): L.append(f"detector evidence: {r['detector']['evidence']}")
        return "\n".join(L)
    crossing = next((r for r in live if r["ts"] >= c["crossed"]), live[-1]) if c["crossed"] else live[-1]
    picked, seen = [], set()
    for r, tag in ((live[0], "first"), (crossing, "the crossing"), (live[-1], "newest")):
        if r["id"] not in seen: picked.append((r, tag)); seen.add(r["id"])
    for r in live:   # then distinct mechanisms: a record whose evidence (or, without any, its observed text) is not one already picked
        if len(picked) >= 6: break
        sig = tuple(r["evidence"]) or r["observed"]
        if r["id"] in seen or any(sig == (tuple(x["evidence"]) or x["observed"]) for x, _ in picked): continue
        picked.append((r, "excerpt")); seen.add(r["id"])
    cnt = lambda key: ", ".join(f"{v} {n}" for n, v in sorted(collections.Counter(key(r) for r in live).items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]))
    costs = [x for r in live for x in r["cost"]]
    out = [f"# failure packet {k['id'] if k else cid} — cluster {cid}", "",
           f"scope: {scope}", f"kind: {c['kind']}", f"contract: {cat.get('contract', '(not in the catalogue)')}", f"symptom: {cat.get('symptom', '')}",
           f"records: {c['confirmed']} confirmed of {c['records']}; episodes: {c['episodes']} ({c['episodes_14d']} in {WINDOW_DAYS}d); critical: {c['critical']}; person-first: {c['person_first']}",
           f"span: {c['first']} .. {c['last']}", f"the rule fired: {c['crossed'] or '(not eligible as of ' + utc(as_of) + ')'} ({c['eligible'] or 'not eligible'})",
           f"claimed: {k['ts'] + ' slot ' + k['slot'] if k else 'no'}", f"writers: {cnt(lambda r: r['writer'])}", f"detectors: {cnt(lambda r: r['detector']['who'])}",
           "known costs (as recorded, never summed): " + ("; ".join(costs) if costs else "none recorded"), "",
           "## records: the first, the crossing, the newest, then distinct excerpts (at most six)", ""]
    for r, tag in picked: out += [rec(r, tag), ""]
    out += ["## the scope's other clusters", ""]
    others = [x for x in cl if x["id"] != cid]
    out += [f"- {x['id']}  {x['kind']}  {x['confirmed']} record(s), {x['episodes_14d']} episode(s) in {WINDOW_DAYS}d" + (f"  ELIGIBLE ({x['eligible']})" if x["eligible"] else "") for x in others] or ["(none)"]
    print("\n".join(out))

def render(cl, all_=False, board=False, as_of=None):
    shown = [c for c in cl if all_ or c["active"]]
    if not cl: print("  (no failures recorded)"); return
    if not shown: print(f"  ({len(cl)} quiet cluster(s), nothing in the last {WINDOW_DAYS} days — --all)"); return
    for c in shown:
        mark = "‼" if c["eligible"] else "·"
        span = f"{c['first'][:16]}..{c['last'][:16]}" if c["first"] != c["last"] else c["first"][:16]
        tail = f"  ELIGIBLE ({c['eligible']}) {claim_word(c, as_of)}" if c["eligible"] else ""
        pf = f"  person-first:{c['person_first']}" if c["person_first"] else ""
        print(f"  {mark} {c['id']}  {c['kind']}  {c['confirmed']} record(s), {c['episodes_14d']} episode(s) in {WINDOW_DAYS}d  {span}{pf}{tail}")
    hid = len(cl) - len(shown)
    if hid and not board: print(f"  ({hid} quiet cluster(s) — --all)")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- import: a board's raised- rows and INSTANCE lines
# A stated time near the head of a note: `2026-09-07 19:0xZ`, `2026-09-09T04:46Z`, `17:2xZ`, `17:12 PDT`,
# `19:0x–19:4xZ` (the first). `x` is a digit the writer did not know: floor to 0, the source's own resolution.
STATED = re.compile(r"(?:(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})[ T])?\b(\d{1,2}):(\d)(\d|x)(?::(\d{2}))?\s*(Z|UTC|PDT|PST)?", re.I)
TZ = {"pdt": 7, "pst": 8, "utc": 0, "z": 0, "": 0}
HEAD = 90   # how far into a note a stated time is looked for; later times ("again 00:59") are leads, not counts
# The marker: INSTANCE as a word of its own (`INSTANCE 17:2xZ`, `THIRD INSTANCE,`). Not the plural — `MY 'FIVE
# INSTANCES' COUNT IS WRONG` is a retraction — and not prose about "INSTANCE lines", which is a brief describing this.
INSTANCE = re.compile(r"\bINSTANCE\b(?!\s+lines?\b)")
def stated_time(text, filed):
    """The time a note states → aware UTC datetime, or None. Dateless: the note's date, or the day before when the
    time of day is over an hour after the filing (`23:3xZ` filed at 00:10Z)."""
    m = STATED.search(text[:HEAD])
    if not m: return None
    date, hh, m1, m2, ss, tz = m.groups()
    hh = int(hh)
    if hh > 23: return None
    mm = int(m1) * 10 + (0 if m2.lower() == "x" else int(m2))
    base = filed if filed else now_dt()
    d = datetime.datetime.strptime(date, "%Y-%m-%d").date() if date else base.date()
    t = datetime.datetime(d.year, d.month, d.day, hh, mm, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc) + datetime.timedelta(hours=TZ[(tz or "").lower()])
    if not date and filed and t > filed + datetime.timedelta(hours=1): t -= datetime.timedelta(days=1)
    return t

# Words that say a person DETECTED it. Not "the owner asked": an ask is what the box was doing when it failed,
# not who saw the failure — `asked` marked four rows person-first that the box's own scripts had caught. Nor
# "the owner would have found": a counterfactual is not a detection.
PERSON = re.compile(r"\b(owner|a person|he)\b(?![^.;:]{0,40}\b(would|could|should|might)\b)[^.;:]{0,40}\b(noticed|caught|found|spotted|flagged|reported|pointed (at|out)|had to (notice|point|prompt|ask|catch|find))\b"
                    r"|\b(the owner's|his) (prompt|nudge|report|correction)\b|\bperson[- ]first\b", re.I)
def stated_detector(text):
    """`person` when the words say a person caught it, with the phrase as the evidence; else unknown, said."""
    m = PERSON.search(text)
    return ("person", m.group(0)) if m else ("unknown", "the row does not say who caught it")

def classify(row, cat):
    """A board row's name → the first catalogue kind whose `match` regex hits, else the row's own family."""
    name = row[len("raised-"):] if row.startswith("raised-") else row
    for kind, k in cat["kinds"].items():
        for pat in k.get("match", []):
            if re.search(pat, name): return kind
    return f"board-row/{row}"

def board_json(repo):
    p = subprocess.run([os.path.join(B, "cc-board"), "json", repo], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if p.returncode != 0: die(f"cc-board json {repo}: {p.stderr.strip() or 'failed'}")
    return json.loads(p.stdout)

def import_board(repo, dry=False):
    cat = catalogue(); d = board_json(repo)
    have = {r["links"].get("source") for r in load(repo) if r.get("links")}
    n = 0
    def put(source, **kw):
        nonlocal n
        if source in have: return
        ids = add_record(repo, source=source, writer="import", dry=dry, **kw); n += 1
        print(f"  {'would write' if dry else 'wrote'} {ids[0]}  {kw['kind']}  {kw['ts'].strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ')}  {source}")
    for row, t in sorted(d.get("tracks", {}).items()):
        kind = classify(row, cat); links = {"row": f"{repo}/{row}"}
        if t.get("pr"): links["pr"] = str(t["pr"])
        brief_path = os.path.join(STATE, repo, row, "task.md")
        try:
            with open(brief_path) as f: brief = f.read()
        except OSError: brief = ""
        if row.startswith("raised-"):    # the row itself is a failure record, filed when it was added
            created = parse_ts(t.get("created") or "") or parse_ts(t.get("updated") or "")
            if created:
                who, ev = stated_detector(t.get("title", "") + "\n" + brief)
                put(f"board:{repo}/{row}", kind=kind, observed=t.get("title", "") or row, ts=created, filed=created,
                    evidence=[f"board:{repo}/{row}"] + ([brief.strip().split("\n")[0][:300]] if brief.strip() else []),
                    detector=who, detector_evidence=ev, links=links)
        for note in t.get("notes", []):   # every INSTANCE line, once each, at the time it states
            msg = note.get("msg", "")
            if not INSTANCE.search(msg): continue
            filed = parse_ts(note.get("ts") or "")
            if not filed: continue
            who, ev = stated_detector(msg)
            put(f"note:{repo}/{row}@{note['ts']}", kind=kind, observed=msg[:400], ts=stated_time(msg, filed) or filed,
                filed=filed, evidence=[f"note:{repo}/{row}@{note['ts']}"], detector=who, detector_evidence=ev, links=links)
        for i, line in enumerate(brief.split("\n"), 1):
            if not INSTANCE.search(line): continue
            created = parse_ts(t.get("created") or "")
            who, ev = stated_detector(line)
            put(f"brief:{repo}/{row}#{i}", kind=kind, observed=line.strip()[:400], ts=stated_time(line, created) or created or now_dt(),
                filed="", evidence=[f"brief:{repo}/{row}#{i}"], detector=who, detector_evidence=ev, links=links)
    print(f"cc-failures import {repo}: {n} new record(s){' (dry)' if dry else ''}, {len(have)} already there")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- metrics
def minutes(a, b):
    """b − a in whole minutes at the minute the stamps are written to; never negative (a writer who rounded the
    stated time up past the filing stamp did not file before it happened)."""
    return max(0, int(((b.replace(second=0) - a.replace(second=0)).total_seconds()) // 60))

def metrics_ledger(scope=None):
    recs = load(scope); live = [r for r in recs if r.get("status") == "confirmed"]
    cl = clusters(recs)
    delays = [minutes(parse_ts(r["ts"]), parse_ts(r["filed"])) for r in live if parse_ts(r.get("filed")) and parse_ts(r["ts"])]
    unk = sum(1 for r in live if r["detector"]["who"] == "unknown"); pf = sum(1 for r in live if r["detector"]["who"] == "person")
    print(f"records: {len(recs)} ({len(live)} confirmed)  clusters: {len(cl)}  eligible: {sum(1 for c in cl if c['eligible'])}")
    if delays: print(f"recording delay (filed - happened, min): median {statistics.median(delays):.0f}, max {max(delays)}, n={len(delays)} ({len(live)-len(delays)} unknown)")
    else: print("recording delay: unknown (no record carries both stamps)")
    if live: print(f"detector: unknown {unk}/{len(live)}, person-first {pf}/{len(live)}, box {len(live)-unk-pf}/{len(live)}")

def metrics_fixture(path):
    cat = catalogue(); items = []
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            for n, line in enumerate(f, 1):
                if line.strip(): items.append(json.loads(line))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e: die(f"fixture {path}: {e}")
    if not items: die(f"fixture {path}: no lines")
    for it in items:
        it["_kind"] = classify(it.get("row", ""), cat)
        filed = parse_ts(it.get("filed", "")); want = parse_ts(it.get("ts", ""))
        got = stated_time(it.get("text", ""), filed) or filed
        it["_ok"] = bool(want and got and got == want)
        it["_delay"] = minutes(want, filed) if want and filed else None
    fm = fs = together = same = 0
    for i in range(len(items)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(items)):
            a, b = items[i], items[j]
            if a["_kind"] == b["_kind"]:
                together += 1
                if a["label"] != b["label"]: fm += 1
            if a["label"] == b["label"]:
                same += 1
                if a["_kind"] != b["_kind"]: fs += 1
    delays = [it["_delay"] for it in items if it["_delay"] is not None]
    print(f"fixture: {len(items)} labelled record(s), {len({it['label'] for it in items})} label(s), {len({it['_kind'] for it in items})} cluster(s) computed")
    print(f"false match rate: {fm}/{together} pairs grouped together carry different labels" + (f" = {fm/together:.0%}" if together else ""))
    print(f"false split rate: {fs}/{same} pairs of one label grouped apart" + (f" = {fs/same:.0%}" if same else ""))
    print(f"true time recovered: {sum(1 for it in items if it['_ok'])}/{len(items)}")
    if delays: print(f"recording delay (filed - happened, min): median {statistics.median(delays):.0f}, max {max(delays)}, n={len(delays)}")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- replay: baseline and candidate on the same frozen events
def read_events(path):
    """The pinned events, in order of when they happened. Every line must carry ts or filed, scope, text and kind or row."""
    evs = []
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            for n, line in enumerate(f, 1):
                if not line.strip(): continue
                try: e = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError: die(f"events {path}:{n}: not JSON")
                e["_n"] = n
                if not (e.get("ts") or e.get("filed")) or not e.get("scope") or not (e.get("kind") or e.get("row")) or not e.get("text"):
                    die(f"events {path}:{n}: needs ts or filed, scope, text, and kind or row")
                evs.append(e)
    except OSError as e: die(f"events {path}: {e}")
    if not evs: die(f"events {path}: no lines")
    return evs

def play(evs, cat_path=None):
    """One detector run over the events: this executable's rule with `cat_path` (default its own catalogue), into a
    temporary ledger. Returns {clusters: {cid: {...fired, control...}}, controls: {name: cid}, errors: [...],
    unknown_kinds: [...]} — everything the comparison and the printer need, nothing from the live ledger."""
    global DIR, CATALOGUE
    import io, contextlib
    T = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-failures-replay."); keep = (DIR, CATALOGUE); DIR = T
    if cat_path: CATALOGUE = cat_path
    err = io.StringIO()
    try:
        cat = catalogue()
        labels, control, playing = {}, {}, []
        for e in sorted(evs, key=lambda e: parse_ts(e.get("ts") or e["filed"]) or now_dt()):
            filed = parse_ts(e.get("filed") or "")
            ts = parse_ts(e.get("ts") or "") or stated_time(e["text"], filed) or filed
            kind = e.get("kind") or classify(e["row"], cat)
            who, ev = (e["detector"], e.get("detector_evidence", "the event says so")) if e.get("detector") else stated_detector(e["text"])
            with contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):
                ids = add_record(e["scope"], kind, e["text"], expected=e.get("expected", ""), evidence=e.get("evidence") or [],
                                 detector=who, detector_evidence=ev, writer=e.get("writer", "replay"), critical=e.get("critical", ""),
                                 status=e.get("status", "confirmed"), ts=ts, filed=filed or "", source=f"replay:{e['_n']}",
                                 links={"row": e["row"]} if e.get("row") else None)
            cid = fpid(fingerprint(e["scope"], kind)); lbl = e.get("label") or f"#{e['_n']}"; labels.setdefault(cid, []).append(lbl)
            if len(ids) > 1: labels.setdefault(fpid(fingerprint(e["scope"], GAP_KIND)), []).append(lbl + "#gap")   # its person-first gap record
            if e.get("control"): control.setdefault(cid, e["control"])
            playing.append((utc(ts), cid, bool(e.get("control"))))
        recs = load()
        errors = []
        for cid, name in control.items():
            real = [t for t, c, is_ctl in playing if c == cid and not is_ctl]
            if real: errors.append(f"control '{name}' shares cluster {cid} with {len(real)} real event(s): a control cluster holds control events only")
        # ask the rule after every event: a cluster's `fired` is the first moment it would have said eligible
        fired, last = {}, {}
        for t in sorted({t for t, _, _ in playing}):
            for c in clusters(recs, parse_ts(t), ks=[]):
                last[c["id"]] = c
                if c["eligible"] and c["id"] not in fired: fired[c["id"]] = {"at": c["crossed"] or t, "seen": t, "why": c["eligible"]}
        out = {}
        for cid, c in last.items():
            out[cid] = {"scope": c["scope"], "kind": c["kind"], "records": c["records"], "confirmed": c["confirmed"], "episodes": c["episodes"],
                        "first": c["first"], "last": c["last"], "labels": labels.get(cid, []), "control": control.get(cid, ""),
                        "fired": fired.get(cid)}
        unknown = sorted({m.group(1) for m in re.finditer(r"'([^']+)' is not in the catalogue", err.getvalue())})
        return {"catalogue": os.path.normpath(CATALOGUE), "events": len(evs), "clusters": out, "errors": errors, "unknown_kinds": unknown}
    finally:
        DIR, CATALOGUE = keep
        shutil.rmtree(T, ignore_errors=True)

def replay(path, cat_path=None, candidate=None, cand_cat=None, as_json=False):
    evs = read_events(path)
    base = play(evs, cat_path)
    if as_json and not (candidate or cand_cat):
        print(json.dumps(base, indent=1)); return 0 if not (base["errors"] or fired_controls(base)) else 1
    cand = None
    if candidate:
        # another cc-failures: its own rule, its own classifier, and its own catalogue when one sits beside it (a checkout);
        # a bare copy (a scratch file) gets the baseline's, so the difference is the code's — or the one named
        own = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(candidate)), "..", "config", "failure-kinds.json")
        cc = cand_cat or (None if os.path.isfile(own) else (cat_path or CATALOGUE))
        p = subprocess.run([candidate, "replay", path, "--json"] + (["--catalogue", cc] if cc else []), capture_output=True, text=True)
        try: cand = json.loads(p.stdout)
        except ValueError: die(f"candidate {candidate}: no replay JSON (rc={p.returncode}): {(p.stderr or p.stdout).strip()[-300:]}")
        cand["exe"] = candidate
    elif cand_cat:
        cand = play(evs, cand_cat); cand["exe"] = os.path.join(B, "cc-failures")
    base["exe"] = os.path.join(B, "cc-failures")
    span = sorted(c["first"] for c in base["clusters"].values())
    ctl = sum(1 for c in base["clusters"].values() if c["control"])
    print(f"replay {os.path.normpath(path)}: {base['events']} event(s), {len(base['clusters'])} cluster(s) of which {ctl} control(s), "
          f"{span[0][:16] if span else '-'} .. {max(c['last'] for c in base['clusters'].values())[:16] if span else '-'}")
    red = False
    for tag, run in (("baseline", base), ("candidate", cand)):
        if not run: continue
        print(f"\n{tag}: {os.path.normpath(run['exe'])}  catalogue {run['catalogue']}")
        for cid, c in sorted(run["clusters"].items(), key=lambda kv: (not kv[1]["fired"], bool(kv[1]["control"]), kv[1]["fired"]["at"] if kv[1]["fired"] else kv[1]["kind"])):
            f = c["fired"]
            if c["control"]:
                print(f"  {'FIRED' if f else 'quiet'}  control '{c['control']}'  {c['kind']}  {c['confirmed']} confirmed of {c['records']}, {c['episodes']} episode(s)"
                      + (f"  — fired {f['at'][:16]} ({f['why']}): A CONTROL MUST STAY QUIET" if f else ""))
                red = red or bool(f)
            elif f:
                print(f"  ‼ {cid}  {c['scope']}  {c['kind']}  fired {f['at'][:16]} ({f['why']})  {c['confirmed']} record(s), {c['episodes']} episode(s)  [{', '.join(c['labels'][:6])}]")
            else:
                print(f"  · {cid}  {c['scope']}  {c['kind']}  quiet  {c['confirmed']} record(s), {c['episodes']} episode(s)")
        if run["unknown_kinds"]: print(f"  kinds outside this catalogue (recorded as their own): {', '.join(run['unknown_kinds'])}")
        for e in run["errors"]: print(f"  ERROR {e}")
        red = red or bool(run["errors"])
    if cand:
        print("\ncandidate vs baseline (the same events):")
        bf = {cid: c for cid, c in base["clusters"].items() if c["fired"]}; cf = {cid: c for cid, c in cand["clusters"].items() if c["fired"]}
        gained = [cid for cid in cf if cid not in bf]; lost = [cid for cid in bf if cid not in cf]
        moved = [(cid, bf[cid]["fired"]["at"], cf[cid]["fired"]["at"]) for cid in cf if cid in bf and cf[cid]["fired"]["at"] != bf[cid]["fired"]["at"]]
        for cid in gained: print(f"  + fires {cid}  {cf[cid]['scope']}  {cf[cid]['kind']}  at {cf[cid]['fired']['at'][:16]} ({cf[cid]['fired']['why']})")
        for cid in lost: print(f"  - no longer fires {cid}  {bf[cid]['scope']}  {bf[cid]['kind']}  (baseline: {bf[cid]['fired']['at'][:16]})")
        for cid, a, b in moved:
            ta, tb = parse_ts(a), parse_ts(b)
            print(f"  ~ {cid}  {cf[cid]['kind']}  crossing moved {a[:16]} → {b[:16]} ({'earlier' if tb < ta else 'later'} by {age(max(ta, tb), min(ta, tb))})")
        if not (gained or lost or moved): print("  no difference: the same clusters fire at the same moments")
        kb, kc = set(base["clusters"]), set(cand["clusters"])
        if kc - kb or kb - kc: print(f"  clusters only in the candidate: {len(kc - kb)}; only in the baseline: {len(kb - kc)} (a kind the catalogue change split or merged)")
    print("\n" + ("RED: a control fired, or the events are not a fixture — not scored" if red else "controls quiet: scored"))
    return 1 if red else 0

def fired_controls(run): return [c for c in run["clusters"].values() if c["control"] and c["fired"]]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- selfcheck: hermetic, its own HOME, ledger and board
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- recurring gate reds (RECURRING, docstring)
RED_KIND = "gate-verdict/red"                       # the lander's record_red (--writer lander) and cc-green's red_seen write it
CASE_MARK = re.compile(r"[✗✘]|(?:^|\s)FAIL\b|^\s*not ok\b")   # a failing CASE, not a tally or a traceback
KNOBS = {"CC_RECURRING_RED_MIN": 3, "CC_RECURRING_RED_WINDOW_H": 72, "CC_RECURRING_RED_COOL_H": 24}
RECUR_DAY_CAP = 2                                   # claims a rolling day, whatever the cases: a burst of flakes buys two
_knobs = {}
def knob(key):
    """A threshold through cc-config (the environment wins there); a value that is not a whole number >= 1 is the default."""
    if key in _knobs: return _knobs[key]
    _knobs[key] = KNOBS[key]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([os.path.join(B, "cc-config"), "get", key, str(KNOBS[key])], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)
        v = int(p.stdout.strip())
        if v >= 1: _knobs[key] = v
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError): pass
    return _knobs[key]
def recur_path(): return os.path.join(DIR, "recurring", "claims.jsonl")   # a subdir: scopes() lists DIR/*.jsonl only

def case_text(line):
    """One red line → the case it names, with what changes run to run (paths, shas, numbers) taken out."""
    s = re.sub(r"^\s*\d+:", "", line)                                   # the excerpt's `grep -n` prefix
    s = re.sub(r"^.*?(?:[✗✘]|\bFAIL\b|\bnot ok\b)\s*", "", s.strip(), count=1)
    s = re.sub(r"(?:~|\.{1,2})?(?:/[\w.@+-]+){2,}/?", "<path>", s)
    s = re.sub(r"\b[0-9a-f]{7,40}\b", "<sha>", s)
    s = re.sub(r"\d+(?:\.\d+)?", "N", s)
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", s).strip(" :—-")[:100]

def red_lines(r):
    """The red lines one gate-verdict/red record carries: its excerpt's red section (both writers keep one), else
    the ✗ pieces of its observed text. The lander writes `check <c> did not pass at the landing of <scope> PR #<n> on
    <sha>: <red line> · <red line>` (records.record_red; the old landing tool said `gate` where it says `check`), and
    both split the same way."""
    for ev in r.get("evidence") or []:
        if isinstance(ev, str) and ev.startswith("excerpt:") and os.path.isfile(ev[8:]):
            try: txt = open(ev[8:], encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read(65536)
            except OSError: break
            body = txt.split("\n\n", 1)[-1].split("\n--- tail ---", 1)[0]
            return body.splitlines()
    return re.split(r" · |; first red line: |: (?=[✗✘])", r.get("observed") or "")

def cases_of_text(lines):
    out = []
    for ln in lines:
        t = case_text(ln) if CASE_MARK.search(ln) else ""
        if len(t) >= 8 and t not in out: out.append(t)
    return out[:5]                                      # a suite that fell over names dozens; the first few are the case

def recurring(scope=None, as_of=None):
    """Every red case in the window: {id, scope, gate, text, landings: {key: ts}, records, excerpts, first, last}.
    A landing is a PR (links.pr), else the tree the red was on — the same PR re-run counts once."""
    as_of = as_of or now_dt(); win = knob("CC_RECURRING_RED_WINDOW_H") * 3600
    by = {}
    for r in load(scope):
        t = parse_ts(r.get("ts"))
        if r.get("kind") != RED_KIND or r.get("status") == "refuted" or not t: continue
        if not 0 <= (as_of - t).total_seconds() < win: continue
        L = r.get("links") or {}
        gate = L.get("gate") or "?"
        land = f"PR #{L['pr']}" if L.get("pr") else f"tree {(L.get('tree') or L.get('source') or r['id'])[:12]}"
        for text in cases_of_text(red_lines(r)):
            cid = "g-" + hashlib.sha1(f"{r['scope']}|{gate}|{text}".encode()).hexdigest()[:8]
            c = by.setdefault(cid, {"id": cid, "scope": r["scope"], "gate": gate, "text": text, "landings": {},
                                    "records": [], "excerpts": [], "first": r["ts"], "last": r["ts"]})
            c["landings"][land] = max(c["landings"].get(land, ""), r["ts"]); c["records"].append(r["id"])
            c["first"], c["last"] = min(c["first"], r["ts"]), max(c["last"], r["ts"])
            c["excerpts"] += [e[8:] for e in r.get("evidence") or [] if isinstance(e, str) and e.startswith("excerpt:")][:1]
    return sorted(by.values(), key=lambda c: (-len(c["landings"]), c["first"]))

def recur_claims():
    p = recur_path()
    if not os.path.isfile(p): return []
    out = []
    for line in open(p):
        try: out.append(json.loads(line))
        except ValueError: pass
    return out

def recur_live(k, as_of):
    """A claim still holding its case: inside the cool-down, or its investigator's journal has no STATUS line yet and
    moved inside two cool-downs (a worker that died without one stops holding then)."""
    t = parse_ts(k.get("ts")); cool = knob("CC_RECURRING_RED_COOL_H") * 3600
    if t and (as_of - t).total_seconds() < cool: return "cool-down"
    pj = os.path.join(STATE, k.get("scope", ""), k.get("track", ""), "progress.md")
    try:
        if time.time() - os.path.getmtime(pj) < 2 * cool and not re.search(r"^STATUS: (DONE|BLOCKED)", open(pj).read(), re.M):
            return "running"
    except OSError: pass
    return ""

def recur_claim(scope=None, as_of=None, dry=False):
    """(claim, None) for the first case over the threshold nobody holds, written once; (None, why) otherwise."""
    as_of = as_of or now_dt(); need = knob("CC_RECURRING_RED_MIN"); ks = recur_claims()
    day = [k for k in ks if parse_ts(k.get("ts")) and 0 <= (as_of - parse_ts(k["ts"])).total_seconds() < DAY]
    over = [c for c in recurring(scope, as_of) if len(c["landings"]) >= need]
    if not over: return None, f"no red case on {need} or more landings"
    if len(day) >= RECUR_DAY_CAP: return None, f"{len(day)} claims in the last day already (the cap)"
    whys = []
    for c in over:
        mine = sorted((k for k in ks if k.get("case") == c["id"]), key=lambda k: k["ts"])
        if mine:
            if recur_live(mine[-1], as_of):
                whys.append(f"{c['id']} held by {mine[-1]['id']} ({recur_live(mine[-1], as_of)})"); continue
            since = [l for l, ts in c["landings"].items() if ts > mine[-1]["ts"]]
            if len(since) < need:
                whys.append(f"{c['id']} red on {len(since)} landing(s) since {mine[-1]['id']}"); continue
        k = {"id": "d-" + hashlib.sha1(f"{c['id']}|{utc(as_of)}".encode()).hexdigest()[:8], "ts": utc(as_of),
             "case": c["id"], "scope": c["scope"], "gate": c["gate"], "text": c["text"],
             "landings": sorted(c["landings"]), "excerpts": sorted(set(c["excerpts"]))[:4],
             "track": f"recurring-red-{c['id'][2:]}"}
        if not dry:
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(recur_path()), exist_ok=True)
            with open(recur_path(), "a") as f:
                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX); f.write(json.dumps(k, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
        return k, None
    return None, "; ".join(whys)

def recur_held(scope, text, as_of=None):
    """The claim line when EVERY case the red text names is one an investigator holds, else ''."""
    as_of = as_of or now_dt(); cs = cases_of_text(re.split(r" · |: (?=[✗✘])|\n", text))
    ks = [k for k in recur_claims() if k.get("scope") == scope and k.get("text") and recur_live(k, as_of)]
    # A prefix either way: cc-land cuts its why at 400 characters, and appends the stale-base note and the log's path to the last case.
    same = lambda t, k: t.startswith(k["text"]) or k["text"].startswith(t)
    hit = [next((k for k in ks if same(t, k)), None) for t in cs]
    if not cs or not all(hit): return ""
    return "held: " + ", ".join(sorted({f"{k['id']} ({k['track']})" for k in hit}))

def selfcheck(*a, **k):
    """The cases are core/tests/selfcheck/cc-failures.py, run in THIS namespace so their stubs and `global`
    rebinds land on the tool as they did when the body was here. Defining them replaces this selfcheck()."""
    path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))), "tests", "selfcheck", "cc-failures.py")
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        exec(compile(fh.read(), path, "exec"), globals())
    return globals()["selfcheck"](*a, **k)

def load_in(env, scope):
    """The ledger as the tool under test reads it — `show ID` prints JSON; the selfcheck asks for the whole scope."""
    p = subprocess.run([os.path.join(B, "cc-failures"), "show", "--scope", scope, "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
    return json.loads(p.stdout) if p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.strip() else []

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- argv
def opts(a, flags, lists=()):
    """--k v pairs → dict (lists collect); bare words → positional. Unknown --flag is usage."""
    out, pos, i = {k: [] for k in lists}, [], 0
    while i < len(a):
        x = a[i]
        if x.startswith("--"):
            k = x[2:]
            if k in ("all", "dry", "json", "once"): out[k] = True; i += 1; continue
            if k not in flags and k not in lists: die(f"unknown option {x}\n{USAGE}")
            if i + 1 >= len(a): die(f"{x} needs a value")
            if k in lists: out[k].append(a[i + 1])
            else: out[k] = a[i + 1]
            i += 2
        else: pos.append(x); i += 1
    return out, pos

USAGE = "usage: cc-failures record|show|eligible|claim|recurring|packet|metrics|replay|import|kinds|selfcheck ...  (the docstring has the flags)"
def as_of(o):
    if not o.get("as-of"): return None
    t = parse_ts(o["as-of"])
    if not t: die(f"--as-of is a UTC stamp like 2026-09-11T17:20Z, got '{o['as-of']}'")
    return t

def main(a):
    if not a: die(USAGE)
    cmd = a[0]; a = a[1:]
    if cmd == "record":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("scope", "kind", "observed", "expected", "detector", "detector-evidence", "writer", "critical", "status", "ts", "corrects"), ("evidence", "cost", "link"))
        for k in ("scope", "kind", "observed"):
            if k not in o: die(f"record needs --{k}\n{USAGE}")
        ts = parse_ts(o["ts"]) if o.get("ts") else None
        if o.get("ts") and not ts: die(f"--ts is a UTC stamp like 2026-09-11T17:20Z, got '{o['ts']}'")
        links = {}
        for kv in o["link"]:
            if "=" not in kv: die(f"--link is k=v, got '{kv}'")
            k, v = kv.split("=", 1); links[k] = v
        status = o.get("status", "confirmed")
        if o.get("corrects"):
            # "Records are immutable; corrections append": the correction names the record, carries the status it
            # now has, and is folded in on every read. It must name a record the ledger holds.
            if "status" not in o: die("--corrects needs --status confirmed|asserted|refuted: the status the record now has")
            if not any(r["id"] == o["corrects"] for r in load(o["scope"])): die(f"no record {o['corrects']} in scope {o['scope']}")
        if o.get("once"):
            if not links.get("source"): die("--once needs --link source=KEY: the key it is written once for")
            have = next((r["id"] for r in load(o["scope"]) if (r.get("links") or {}).get("source") == links["source"]), None)
            if have: print(f"already {have}"); return
        ids = add_record(o["scope"], o["kind"], o["observed"], expected=o.get("expected", ""), evidence=o["evidence"],
                         detector=o.get("detector", "unknown"), detector_evidence=o.get("detector-evidence", ""),
                         writer=o.get("writer", "session"), cost=o["cost"], links=links, critical=o.get("critical", ""),
                         status=status, ts=ts, corrects=o.get("corrects"))
        print(" ".join(ids))
    elif cmd in ("show", "eligible"):
        o, pos = opts(a, ("scope", "as-of"))
        recs = load(o.get("scope"))
        if cmd == "show" and o.get("json"):
            print(json.dumps(recs, indent=1)); return
        if cmd == "show" and pos:
            for r in recs:
                if r["id"] == pos[0] or r["cluster"] == pos[0]: print(json.dumps(r, indent=1))
            return
        cl = clusters(recs, as_of(o))
        if cmd == "eligible":
            for c in cl:
                if c["eligible"]: print(f"{c['id']}\t{c['scope']}\t{c['kind']}\t{c['eligible']}\t{c['episodes_14d']} episode(s)\t{c['first'][:16]}..{c['last'][:16]}\t{claim_word(c, as_of(o))}")
        else: render(cl, o.get("all"), as_of=as_of(o))
    elif cmd == "claim":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("scope", "as-of"))
        k = claim_one(o.get("scope"), as_of(o), dry=bool(o.get("dry")))
        if not k: sys.exit(1)
        print(f"{k['id']}\t{k['cluster']}\t{k['scope']}\t{k['kind']}\t{k['why']}\t{k['slot']}")
    elif cmd == "packet":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("as-of",))
        if len(pos) != 1: die("packet needs a claim or cluster id")
        packet(pos[0], as_of(o))
    elif cmd == "board":   # what `cc board failures <repo>` execs: the board's own heading, then the scope's clusters
        o, pos = opts(a, ("as-of",))
        if not pos: die("board needs a repo")
        print(f"\n\033[1m{pos[0]}\033[0m  failures  (cc-failures; the rule: critical, or {EPISODES_NEEDED} episodes in {WINDOW_DAYS} days)")
        render(clusters(load(pos[0]), as_of(o)), board=True, as_of=as_of(o)); print()
    elif cmd == "metrics":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("scope",))
        if pos: metrics_fixture(pos[0])
        else: metrics_ledger(o.get("scope"))
    elif cmd == "replay":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("catalogue", "candidate", "candidate-catalogue"))
        if len(pos) > 1: die("replay takes one events file")
        for k in ("catalogue", "candidate", "candidate-catalogue"):
            if o.get(k) and not os.path.isfile(o[k]): die(f"--{k}: no such file {o[k]}")
        sys.exit(replay(pos[0] if pos else EVENTS, o.get("catalogue"), o.get("candidate"), o.get("candidate-catalogue"), as_json=bool(o.get("json"))))
    elif cmd == "import":
        o, pos = opts(a, ())
        if len(pos) != 1: die("import needs a repo")
        import_board(pos[0], dry=bool(o.get("dry")))
    elif cmd == "kinds":
        cat = catalogue()
        print(f"catalogue v{cat.get('version')}: {os.path.normpath(CATALOGUE)}")
        for k, v in cat["kinds"].items(): print(f"  {k}\n      contract: {v.get('contract','')}\n      symptom:  {v.get('symptom','')}")
        print("critical reasons: " + ", ".join(f"{k} ({v})" for k, v in cat["critical"].items()))
    elif cmd == "recurring":
        o, pos = opts(a, ("scope", "as-of", "text"))
        sub = pos[0] if pos else "show"
        if sub == "claim":
            k, why = recur_claim(o.get("scope"), as_of(o), dry=bool(o.get("dry")))
            if not k: print(f"cc-failures: nothing to claim: {why}", file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(1)
            print(json.dumps(k, ensure_ascii=False))
        elif sub == "held":
            if not o.get("scope") or "text" not in o: die("recurring held needs --scope S --text TEXT")
            h = recur_held(o["scope"], o["text"], as_of(o))
            if not h: sys.exit(1)
            print(h)
        elif sub == "show":
            need, ks = knob("CC_RECURRING_RED_MIN"), recur_claims()
            for c in recurring(o.get("scope"), as_of(o)):
                k = max((k for k in ks if k.get("case") == c["id"]), key=lambda k: k["ts"], default=None)
                print(f"{c['id']}\t{c['scope']}\t{c['gate']}\t{len(c['landings'])} landing(s){' ≥ ' + str(need) if len(c['landings']) >= need else ''}"
                      f"\t{k['id'] + ' ' + k['ts'] if k else 'unclaimed'}\t{c['text']}")
        else: die("recurring [show] | claim [--dry] | held --scope S --text TEXT")
    elif cmd == "selfcheck":
        sys.exit(selfcheck())
    else: die(USAGE)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
